{
  "dom_id": "step-q556439",
  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "Which of the following is the best estimate for $\\sqrt{73}?$",
  "worked_solution": "To estimate $\\sqrt{73},$ we first find the two perfect squares closest to $73.$\n\nThe closest perfect squares are $64={8}^{2}$ and $81={9}^{2}.$\n\nSince $64<73<81,$ we know that the square root of $73$ lies between $8$ and $9.$ This tells us that $7.6$ and $36.5$ are incorrect estimates.\n\nBecause $73$ is slightly closer to $81$ than to $64$ (the distance to $64$ is $9,$ and the distance to $81$ is $8$), we expect $\\sqrt{73}$ to be near the middle of the interval.\n\nWe can test the plausible choices by squaring them to see which one results in a value closest to $73:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{8.2}^{2} & =67.24 \\\\ {8.5}^{2} & =72.25 \\\\ {8.9}^{2} & =79.21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that ${8.5}^{2}=72.25$ is very close to $73.$\n\nTherefore, the best estimate for $\\sqrt{73}$ is $8.5.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
